# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Visual Studio / VS Code
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo

# Node (only if you later add a test suite)
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Local scratch
*.local
*.bak
*.tmp

# Substance packs that carry synopsis prose (scripts/fetch-substance.js --include-prose).
# A synopsis is expressive text, not a fact, and this repository is public -- so the prose pack
# stays local while the tag-only pack beside it is committed as the scoring evidence of record.
evidence/*.prose.json

# Recorded raw API responses. Committing these makes a fetch run replayable, which is often worth
# it -- but they can carry synopsis prose too, so they are opt-in via `git add -f`.
evidence/raw-*.json

# score-snapshot.js output. Diagnostic, not evidence -- every value in it is DERIVED (gm, indices,
# content rating) and fully regenerable on demand from any commit (`node scripts/score-snapshot.js`)
# plus a browser, unlike the fact/substance evidence pairs above, which are the only record of what
# an external source actually said on a given date. At ~1.6MB per snapshot and several per batch,
# committing these across a 2,508-work run would balloon the repo for no lasting benefit -- the
# batch commit message and its evidence files are the durable record; the snapshot diff shown while
# working is the point, not the file itself.
evidence/snapshots/
